There are a lot of compilation issues when I try to compile the code. My tests work but I want to cpmpile the system fully. The issues are following: 1. there are issues with md/ some methods are called that dont exist; maybe the orderbook related and maybe more. 2. There are issued with CPU pinning 3. the APIs for different exchanges shall have their params or placeholders such as via some config file to be able to retrieve L2 data and make calls. We have issues with all these. We need to make sure the code compiles fully and can be dockerised in totality later. The aim is to dockerise it in totality and then be able to run it on an EC2 instance. 


Next, we need to make sure that the backtesting framework is robust and can handle different types of strategies, including ML/DNN based strategies. This means we need to have a clear interface for strategy implementation and ensure that the backtesting engine can simulate market conditions accurately. The backtest shall not use simulated data but rather replay historical data from the SQLite database to ensure realism. 


Furthermore, we need to have a proper README file that explains how to compile the code, run the tests, and then dockerise it. The README should also explain how to set up the config files for different exchanges and how to enable/disable features like CPU pinning, multi-threading, etc. 

Finally, we need to ensure that the code is modular enough to allow for easy addition of new exchanges in the future. This means having a clear interface for exchange APIs and ensuring that the data normalization process can handle data from any exchange seamlessly.  

